  "talk": [
    {
      "id": "talk-prime-inner-ward",
      "npcs": ["page", "sacristan"],
      "watch": "prime",
      "lines": [
        "Is there wax to spare? The hall burned three candles down to the dish last night, and I am to fetch more before anybody sits.",
        "There is wax for the altar and there is wax for the hall, and they are not the same wax. Ask me properly and I will think about it.",
        "Then I am asking properly. Slowly, and with my cap off."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-sext-outer-ward",
      "npcs": ["baker-lad", "well-wife"],
      "watch": "sext",
      "lines": [
        "Two buckets for the trough and one for the dough, she says, and not off the bottom of the well this time. She says it tastes of the bottom.",
        "The bottom of the well is where the water is, boy. Tell her the rope is as long as it was yesterday and so is my patience.",
        "I will tell her you said so. I will not tell her how you said it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-sext-inner-ward",
      "npcs": ["tiring-woman", "maid"],
      "watch": "sext",
      "lines": [
        "The blue linen came back from the wash with a scorch on the hem. A hand's width, right where it shows when she sits.",
        "Then the blue goes to the bottom of the chest and the green comes out. She will not look at a hem if the sleeves are right.",
        "She looks at everything. That is the whole trouble with her, and the whole reason we still have our places."
      ]
    }
  ]
